+# Full study — S5-CLM-00003535
+
+## Mathematical reading
+
+The frozen statement is Boshernitzan's density-modulo-one theorem.  It takes
+an everywhere-positive real sequence, excludes bounded sequences, and imposes
+the sublacunary ratio limit.  The exceptional set consists exactly of those
+real multipliers whose orbit in the unit additive circle fails to be dense;
+the asserted Hausdorff dimension is zero.
+
+## Semantic identity
+
+The source locator is the pinned `Problem10_6.lean` block at bytes 3533–4027.
+The declaration and declaration-type hashes are copied from the immutable
+workset record.  The target surface expands all binders directly, with no
+local abbreviations, coercion wrappers, notation, aliases, or import
+substitution.  The required provider spelling remains in each Lean file's
+provenance comment, while executable compilation uses `Mathlib`.
+
+## Proof/composition/trust study
+
+The provider file is in the FC-SORRY cohort.  Its `sorryAx` is a negative
+proof-authority signal and is not included in the target proof graph.  The
+target graph therefore separates source provenance, hypotheses, bidirectional
+semantic transport, and the root application.  Master is responsible for
+replacing the worker's declared environment with a recomputed kernel trace.
+
+## Readable reconstruction
+
+The readable ledger names every required root-relevant node and maps it to one
+content-addressed fragment.  The reverse map retains hypotheses, inference,
+output, formal anchor, downstream uses, exceptional cases, and trust boundary.
+Two independent reviewers are recorded; deletion mutations are required to
+fail before the R0 decision is accepted.
+
+## Negative fixture and strict dominance
+
+`THM-M-0387` is treated only as the pinned incomplete H1/M2/R0 negative
+fixture.  This package adds the semantic environment, semantic-substitution
+mutation outcomes, and cold-from-source replay dimensions required by the
+strict-dominance certificate.  It is not used as a proof precedent.
